# Build output
/target
**/*.rs.bk

# OS / editor noise
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
*~

# Crash dumps from MSYS-hosted shells
*.stackdump

# MSYS-mangled path artifacts.
#
# `sh -c` on Windows resolves to git-bash, whose MSYS layer flattens an absolute
# Windows path passed inside a command string ("C:\Users\...\env.txt") into a
# single relative token, substituting U+F03A for the drive colon. A redirect in a
# test command then writes that token into the crate directory. The emitting
# tests are POSIX-gated (see notifications/hooks.rs), so these should no longer
# appear -- this rule is the backstop, because the files carry a full environment
# dump including the user name and any secret-bearing variables.
**

# Sweep / scratch
/.sweep-scratch/
sweep-*.log

# Python bytecode from the asset generators
__pycache__/
*.pyc
